#---
# purpose: "an opaque join of function values whose every branch is ill-typed arithmetic is rejected at compile time"
# expect: diagnostic
# diagnostic.code: spec/violation
#---
#
# # opaque_fn_all_divergent
#
# Both join members add `1`/`2` to the atom `:bad`. Kernel's arithmetic
# `@spec`s accept only numbers, so each body is a provable spec violation at
# a user callsite and compilation fails with `spec/violation` before any
# backend runs. The verdict is a compile-time fact shared by run, interp, and
# build, so the three paths agree by construction.
def stop_a(_), do: :bad + 1
def stop_b(_), do: :bad + 2
def invoke(f), do: f.(1)

def main() do
  f = case Process.heap_alloc_stats()[:allocs] == 0 do
    true -> stop_a
    _ -> stop_b
  end
  dbg(invoke(f))
  dbg(:unreachable)
end
